{"strongs": "H2659", "word": "חָפֵר", "translit": "cha.pher", "root": "חפר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be abashed, ashamed", "definition": "II. [ חָפֵר ] verb be abashed, ashamed ( ᵑ7 חֲפַר Prov 13:5 , מַחְפְּרָנָא one causing shame Prov 19:26 Syriac , especially Aph`el be ashamed, put to shame ; Arabic be bashful , shy, bashful ; Ethiopic be ashamed, blush ) — Qal Perfect 3 feminine singular חָֽפְרָה Jer 50:12 וְחָֽפְרָה consecutive Isa 24:23 וְחָפֵ֑רָה Jer 15:9 חָֽפְרוּ Ps 71:24 וְחָֽפְרוּ consecutive Mic 3:7 Imperfect יַחְפְּרוּ Ps 35:4 + 4 t.; יֶחְפָּ֑רוּ Ps 34:6 וַיֶּחְפָּ֑רוּ Job 6:20 תַּחְפְּרוּ Isa 1:29 — be abashed, ashamed , said of face Ps 34:6 (avoided by looking to ׳ י ); elsewhere always || בּוֺשׁ , of enemies of righteousness Ps 71:24 ; Ps 35:4 ; Ps 35:26 ; Ps 40:15 = Ps 70:3 ; Ps 83:18 of idolaters Isa 1:29 diviners Mic 3:7 of distressed Jerusalem Jer 15:9 so of Babylon Jer 50:12 of moon Isa 24:33 be put to shame (disappointment), of caravans looking for water Job 6:20 . Hiph`il Perfect הֶחְפִּיר Isa 33:9 Imperfect יַחְפִּיר Prov 13:5 תַּחְפִּ֫ירִי Isa 54:4 Participle מַחְפִּיר Prov 19:26 — display shame , figurative of Lebanon Isa 33:9 (|| קָמַ֑ל 'dried up' Che ); of Israel Isa 54:4 (|| בּוֺשׁ Qal); of an unfilial son, cause shame Prov 19:26 (|| מֵבִישׁ ); compare Prov 13:5 of wicked (|| יבאישׁ : see באשׁ Hiph`il above).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3018')\">BDB3018</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2659')\">H2659</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3017')\">BDB3017</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3019')\">BDB3019</entry></div><p> II. [<bdbheb>חָפֵר</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be abashed, ashamed</highlightword> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>חֲפַר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 13:5\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(20,13,5)\">Prov 13:5</ref>, <bdbheb>מַחְפְּר